// hopper_clog_cyl_analytic_tc1_caps_sanity_gas.prm   (copy of hopper_clog_cyl_analytic_tc1_caps_gas.prm + the new END-OF-STEP fluid sanity sweep)
// [Claude, 2026-09-20] RERUN of job 4251203 (analytic, tc=1d, rod caps; survived 8136 steps, fluid blow-up at the slit throat (378.5,23.5,24.5), first |u|=0.53 at step 8120) with PhysicsParameters.fluidSanity* ON from step 3000:
// max|u| 0.3, rho window 0.1-1.9, max|f_i| 2.0, fill tolerance 0.05 + the extra checks (|excess mass| 1.0, face-neighbour |du| 0.2 / |drho| 0.3, liquid touching gas) and a [FLUID-STATS] extrema line every 100 steps. Report-only (no abort).
// Goal: catch the onset of the throat instability earlier than the 0.5 precursor and see whether the neighbour-jump / excess-mass / topology checks fire first.
// hopper_clog_cyl_analytic_tc1_caps_gas.prm   (GENERATED by hand from hopper_clog_cyl_short_analytic_tc1_fluidscan_gas.prm)
// [Claude, 2026-09-20] CAP TEST: the crash-prone configuration (analytic closed-form contacts, collisionTimeFactor 1; aborted at steps 3599, 3493, 3517 in three fresh runs) with ARTIFICIAL CAPS on the rods (hydro force 1.0,
// torque 5.0, velocity 0.15, angular velocity 0.05, contact overlap 1.0) and the per-step fluid scan. Question: is the excessive rod force/motion (launch) the cause of the crashes or only a symptom? If the run survives
// far beyond ~3500 steps the launches were the problem; if it dies later with [NaN-SCAN]/fluid garbage the fluid side is the root. 9000 steps. The [RodCaps] log line gives the cap-hit counts.
// hopper_clog_cyl_short_analytic_tc1_fluidscan_gas.prm   (GENERATED by hand from hopper_clog_cyl_short_analytic_tc1_gas.prm)
// [Claude, 2026-09-20] FLUID-SIDE DIAGNOSTIC rerun of the crash-prone analytic/tc=1d configuration (aborted at steps 3599 and 3493 in jobs 4250977/4251049 after a rod got a raw MEM hydro force of ~4.6e21):
// per-step PDF scan of all liquid/interface cells for steps 3000..6000 (denseNanScan + highVelocityPrecursorThreshold 0.5, logs cell classification incl. former-moving-obstacle) and the new
// [MEM-GARBAGE-LINK] log in SimpleBB.h (any link with |pdf| > 10: cell flags, fill, density, all populations, neighbour flags). Floater history OFF.
// hopper_clog_cyl_frontblock_pidon_2node_gas.prm   (GENERATED by gen_hopper_clog_cyl_prm.py -- edit the script, not this file)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// [Claude, 2026-09-19] "HOPPER" CLOGGING SETUP, CYLINDER VERSION (THESIS_PLAN.md item 3/4). NOT RUN YET.
// Companion of the sphere hopper (prms/hopper_clog_pidon_2node_frontblock_gas.prm, same channel/pillars/PID/probes/VTK): two cylindrical pillars centred on the
// Y walls (X=384, radius 12, central gap 16 LU, plan view "|) (|") -- but the debris are CYLINDERS, diameter:length = 1:3 (r=3, L=18; the sphere's
// 6 LU cross-section), LONG AXIS ALONG Y (across the channel), released together from a block pressed against the pillars.
//
// KEY GEOMETRIC FACT: the rod length 18 is LONGER than the 16 LU gap. A rod lying along Y therefore cannot pass the gap broadside: it has to rotate its axis towards the flow.
// Expect jamming of rods across the opening (log-jam like) rather than the free arching of the sphere hopper -- a different mechanism (rotation-limited passage).
//
// POPULATION: 406 rods = 2 across Y x 7 layers x 29 rows in X (pitch X/Y/Z = 7/20/7.52, >= 1 LU surface clearance rod-rod / wall / floor,
// checked exactly for parallel cylinders). Only 2 rods of length 18 fit across the 40 LU channel, and each rod is ~4.5x the volume of a sphere, hence far fewer than the 1015
// spheres (kept: the same 29 rows, i.e. the same block length). densityRatio {0.5,1.0,1.2} = 116/174/116, stratified by height like the sphere version (1.2 low, 1.0
// mid, 0.5 in the top two layers; the top layer's axis sits at the waterline Z=49.13, half submerged).
// Block X in [169.0,371.0], front row 1.04 LU (surface to pillar surface, exact rectangle-disc distance) from the pillar cylinders.
// All rods are held FIXED for 2000 steps (settlingSteps, no startInactive) and then released together; clearance >= 1 LU so [RELEASE-OVERLAP] cannot fire at release.
//
// CONTACT MODEL: useAnalyticalContactDetection true (Cylinder x Cylinder = analytical Kodam+Guo HYBRID, usePureAnalyticalCylinder false keeps the GJK/EPA fallback;
// Cylinder x pillar/wall analytic regardless) + useContactFilterOwnerTiebreak true; every experimental contact/buoyancy fix explicitly OFF (see ModelParameters) EXCEPT useTightLayer1 (ON, user request 2026-09-20: the capsule/segment-distance pre-filter for Cylinder x Cylinder; near-parallel false-positive fix is in PaperAnalyticalContacts.h + an always-on capsule bound).
// Friction/restitution as in the sphere hopper (0.5 / 0.5).
//
// FLOW/UNITS: identical to the sphere hopper (PID on, target 0.04, water Z=49.13, Z=180 headroom, <768,40,180> / <64,20,30> = 144 ranks / 2 nodes).
// CAVEATS: the upstream clog probes (X=336) sit inside the rod block (unusable as a clog signal, as in the sphere case); the fluid VTK is cropped to X 128..640, Z 0..100
// (the rods are unfiltered); the [CylComputation] contact-path diagnostics make logs very large (the 100-floater sediment run's log was 594 MB) -- expect a big .out file.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 64, 20, 30 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 0, 0 >;
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 false;
   snapshotFrequency             5000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <768, 40, 180>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.0;
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0.04;
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
   enabled                     true;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting     false;
   timesteps         9000;
   Re                3100;
   Fr                1.31;
   We                15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits false;
   denseNanScanEnabled            true;    // per-step PDF scan of every liquid/interface cell in the window below (NaN/Inf abort + precursors)
   denseNanScanFromStep           3000;
   denseNanScanToStep             9000;
   highVelocityPrecursorThreshold 0.5;     // [HIGH-VELOCITY-PRECURSOR] for any liquid/interface cell with |u| > 0.5 (mean flow 0.04): a finite garbage PDF shows up here
   fluidSanityEnabled             true;    // [Claude, 2026-09-20] end-of-step sweep over liquid/interface cells (see SimulationParams.h)
   fluidSanityFromStep            3000;
   fluidSanityToStep              9000;
   fluidSanityEveryNSteps         1;
   fluidSanityMaxVelocity         0.17;    // [Claude, 2026-09-21] 0.17 = lattice Mach number 0.3 (Kruger 2017 Sect. 7.2); job 4251480 ran with 0.3 (Ma 0.52) -- accuracy warning, not a collapse threshold
   fluidSanityDensityMin          0.1;
   fluidSanityDensityMax          1.9;
   fluidSanityMaxPopulation       2.0;
   fluidSanityFillTolerance       0.05;
   fluidSanityMaxExcessMass       1.0;
   fluidSanityMaxNeighbourVelocityJump 0.2;
   fluidSanityMaxNeighbourDensityJump  0.3;
   fluidSanityCheckTopology       true;
   fluidSanityStatsEveryNSteps    100;
   fluidSanityAbortAbove          0;       // report only
   // no gravityOverride -- dynamically computed, see the extreme-clog prm's header
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;   // never opened -- see avgParticleDiameterOverride below
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   avgParticleDiameterOverride 8.001943372119138;
   dxSIOverride                0.000362694127490625;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.5;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
   collisionTimeFactor 1;   // tc = factor * 8.0019 LBM steps; default 4 -> k x (4/factor)^2
}

CylinderPillars
{
   // axes ON the Y walls: half of each cylinder lies outside the domain (harmless). Z is an arbitrary reference point on the vertical axis.
   CylinderPillar { center < 384, 0, 45 >; radius 12; }
   CylinderPillar { center < 384, 40, 45 >; radius 12; }
}

FloatingCylinders
